22:["$","$L34",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is AI automation?","answer":"AI automation uses artificial intelligence to run business processes end to end — reading inputs, making decisions, and taking action — instead of relying only on fixed, rule-based scripts. It combines the reliability of automation with the flexibility of AI, so you can automate work that used to require a person, including the exceptions that break traditional tools."},{"question":"AI automation vs traditional automation or RPA — what's the difference?","answer":"Traditional automation and RPA follow hard-coded rules: fast and reliable, but brittle — they break the moment something is off-script or arrives as a PDF, email, or free text. AI automation adds reasoning on top, so it can read unstructured inputs, classify and decide, and handle exceptions without dumping the case back on a human."},{"question":"What can you automate in my business?","answer":"Business processes (onboarding, approvals, reconciliation), document workflows (invoices, contracts, forms), marketing and sales ops (lead routing, enrichment, follow-up), system integrations between your ERP/CRM/tools, and industrial or process automation on the factory floor. We scope by ROI — we automate the bottleneck that eats the most time first."},{"question":"How much does AI automation cost?","answer":"A focused automation sprint typically starts around $15K; multi-process programs scale from there depending on the number of workflows, integrations, and the AI involved. We start with a discovery to map your processes and quote a fixed scope for the first one. Senior nearshore engineers keep it a fraction of a US agency."},{"question":"Can you connect it to our existing tools (ERP, CRM, and the rest)?","answer":"Yes — integration is most of the work. We connect your ERP, CRM, help desk, databases, and SaaS tools via API or platforms like Make, Zapier, n8n, and Power Automate, so data flows automatically with no copy-paste. The automation runs inside your real stack; it doesn't replace it."},{"question":"How is AI automation different from AI agents?","answer":"AI automation runs a defined process with AI handling the decisions inside it. An AI agent is fully autonomous — it plans and acts toward a goal across your systems. Automation is the reliable plumbing; agents are the next step up. We build both, and often combine them: automations for the repeatable flow, agents for the open-ended work."},{"question":"Do you offer AI automation consulting, or only implementation?","answer":"Both. Every engagement starts with AI automation consulting: we map your processes, find the highest-ROI bottleneck, and hand you a costed automation plan. Then the same senior nearshore team builds, integrates, and monitors it in production. You can stop at the roadmap — most teams keep us through delivery."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask about AI automation.","fill":true}]
